__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.orig

# ⛔ ROCKSTAR-DERIVED KEY MATERIAL — DELIBERATELY NOT VERSIONED.
# The standing non-negotiable is that we never ship a byte of Rockstar data or key material. Git
# history is a ONE-WAY DOOR: once this blob is committed it survives every later `git remote add`
# and push, and removing it from history is a rewrite. The file stays on disk and still ships by
# whatever distribution route is chosen (maintainer decision 2026-07-27, option A) - it simply is not
# in version control. Reversible: delete this line if versioning it is the deliberate call.
resources/magic.dat

# ⛔ NOT PUBLISHED. Files stay on disk (nothing is deleted) - they are simply not in the public
# repo, because each is a distinct exposure:
#  * the archived unpack_magic helper - reads a resource out of a local third-party tool's DLL and
#    hardcodes the author's own desktop path. Publishing it would contradict the ZERO-third-party-tool-
#    affiliation rule in the most literal way possible, and leak a personal path.
#  * findkeys / recover_keys / try_variants / derive_entry / probe_* - key-RECOVERY research.
#    Publishing the methodology is a larger exposure than shipping the tool, and serves no user.
#  * yft2xml_pre_vehicle.py - a superseded snapshot; noise in a public tree.
# Remove this block only as a deliberate decision, not to make a push go through.
_archive/

# The churn gate's baseline is DERIVED FROM THE OPERATOR'S OWN INSTALL (asset names + output
# hashes from their extraction), and it is machine-specific by design. Same rule as every other
# game-derived artifact here: it lives in the project folder, never in the repo.
_regress_baseline.json
